  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Malay names have no family name: a given name, then bin (son of) or binti (daughter of) and the father's name, as in Ahmad Faiz bin Ismail or Nur Aisyah binti Abdullah. People shorten it to the given name (Faiz) or given name plus father's name (Faiz Ismail). Many men's names start with Muhammad or Mohd. Chinese Malaysians put the family name first and spell it in their family's dialect, Cantonese, Hokkien or Hakka (Wong, Tan, Lim, Chin), and many add an English name in front (Jason Wong Wei Liang). Indian Malaysians, mostly Tamil, carry their father's name after their own, sometimes written a/l (anak lelaki, son of) or a/p (anak perempuan, daughter of). The peoples of Sabah and Sarawak have their own naming customs not yet covered here.",
